  "body": "### Summary\nAs a Mac session, I want the hosted list-look tests to pass on every simulator we use, so that a Duo run is not red because of a test assumption.\n\n### Scope\n- `ListLookHostedTests` sets the window to 402 × 874 (`ListLookHostedTests.swift:70`, `:229`) and expects `row.frame.width == 402` (`:214`).\n- On the iPhone Duo simulator (iOS 27.2), every list's rows are 318 pt wide (measured during #1306 round 0, on Catégories, Plus and the others), so the dense test fails 12 times. This predates #1306.\n- Fix: compare against the width the rows actually get (the host view's width), or skip that check on that idiom.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The suite is green on the iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone Duo simulators.\n- [ ] The test still fails if a dense row gets the card inset back.\n\nFound while testing #1306 (w693, reviewed by r1306).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
